          "text": "filename: docs/choir-summary.md\n# Choir Rehearsal Summary\n\n## Key Points\n- The choir rehearsal took place on Tuesday evening at the church hall with fourteen singers in attendance.\n- Marta led the warm-up session, focusing on breathing techniques for ten minutes.\n- Owen arrived late due to a delayed bus, but offered to print fresh copies of the score before Friday.\n- The group began with the folk song \"Down by the River.\"\n- Priya highlighted that the altos tend to rush during the second verse, prompting the group to slow the tempo and clap the rhythm together.\n- Marta suggested marking breath points in everyone's sheet music to improve performance.\n- The tenors continue to struggle with a high note near the end of the piece.\n- Priya will book the hall for two additional rehearsals in March.\n- The choir agreed to schedule the spring concert for the second Saturday of April.\n- Tea and biscuits were provided by the hall committee.\n- The next rehearsal is scheduled for seven thirty sharp.\n\n## Next Steps\n- Owen will print fresh copies of the score by Friday.\n- Priya will book the hall for two extra rehearsals in March.\n- The choir will continue working on the high note in the tenors' section.\n- All members should bring a pencil and a water bottle to the next rehearsal.\n- The group will focus on refining the rhythm and breath points in the upcoming sessions.",
